What Is It ?
============
Package kz, named after its creator, Karel Zimmer, contains scripts for
installing and managing Red Hat and Red Hat-based systems such as Rocky Linux.

Also installs (dependencies)
============================
dialog          - A utility for creating TTY dialog boxes (TUI)
polkit          - An authorization framework
psmisc          - Utilities for managing processes on your system (fuser)
python3         - Python v.rr (e.g. 3.12) interpreter
rsync           - A program for synchronizing files over a network
epel-release    - Extra Packages for Enterprise Linux repository configuration
xdg-user-dirs   - Handles user special directories
zenity          - Display graphical dialog boxes from shell scripts (GUI)

How To Use
==========
For how to use this package see Checklist installation.
Checklist installation can be found on the site https://karelzimmer.nl/en,
under Linux.

